# Consoleri design system

Before changing UI styles, read `design-system/USAGE.md` and `design-system/DESIGN.md`.

## Source of truth

- Canonical tokens: `design-system/tokens.css` (Open Design charter: `--bg`, `--accent`, …)
- App C-extensions: `design-system/tokens.app-extensions.css`
- Tailwind bridge: import `@consoleri/design-system/tailwind` only via `app.css` — do not add a second `@theme` in feature files
- Hex for canvas/xterm: `apps/desktop/src/renderer/src/theme/hex.ts` (synced with `design-system/hex.json`)

## Do

- Use semantic utilities: `bg-bg`, `bg-surface`, `text-fg`, `text-muted`, `border-border`, `bg-accent`
- Prefer `components/ui` primitives for buttons, modals, fields
- Put product-only CSS vars in `tokens.app-extensions.css`, not in page components

## Avoid

- Arbitrary hex in `className` (`bg-[#…]`, `border-[#…]`)
- Parallel palettes (`gray-*` / `blue-600` as brand colors)
- Editing `tailwind-v4.css` values by hand — regenerate from `tokens.css`
- Treating `brand.json` as runtime CSS source of truth
